{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Of Chanoch, the family of the Chanochi</b> – Perhaps just as the land was divided among the tribes according to the opinion of our Sages (Bava Batra 122a), and the tribe of Shimon, the smaller one, took an equal portion to the tribe of Judah, the larger one — portion for portion — so too [the land] was divided among the fathers' houses of those who went down to Egypt, and they made four portions from the inheritance of Reuben, and the portion of the family of the Chanochi was equal to the portion of the family of the Pallui and the Chezroni and the Karmi, even though they are not equal in the number of names to their head-count. And this is the reason for this census, that they counted the families of those who went down to Egypt and did not mention \"לגלגלתם\" (by head-count), even though he does mention their number in the aggregate. And what he said, \"to the many you shall increase his inheritance\" (Numbers 26:54), refers to the sons of the families who each received according to his count, to their head-count. And because of this, in the book of Joshua he mentions in the division of the land \"למשפחתיהם\" (by their families): \"And the lot for the tribe of the children of Judah was by their families\" (Joshua 15:1), and so in all of them. Or the reason for \"למשפחתיהם\" may be [that it refers] to all the families of the tribe, or that they divided the land by their families and each and every family had its portion in one place and it would not intermix with another family — and this is what seems correct in my eyes."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:08:47.859110283Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}